  "body": "Stacked on #798\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What changed\nBefore every `G0 A..`, the PathPilot post lifts Z to the top of travel (`G53 G0 Z0`), and a `G30` can move A too. Until now nothing checked that the tool there clears what turns under it. The program gate now does.\n\n- **New gate clause** (`crates/app/src/posting_index_swing.rs`, wired into `verification_report`). It checks every op whose machine has a rotary about X that turns the work.\n  - **Tip height:** the tool tip sits at `nose_to_axis - tool length`, where tool length is cutter + shank + holder, with a modelled body counted.\n  - **Swept radius:** the farthest vertex from the A line (through WCS Y0 Z0, along X) of the setup's stock, the parts, and the tagged fixtures that turn with the work. Fixed fixtures are left out.\n  - **Refusal:** if the clearance is under 5 mm, the post is refused naming the op, the A, the tip height, the swept radius and the clearance, e.g. `FLAT: the A90.000 index turns the work under the tool - at the safe Z the tip of EM 1/4 (...) is ... mm above the A centerline, the stock, part and turning fixtures sweep 13.470 mm, a clearance of 3.000 mm against the 5.0 mm needed`.\n- **Machine file statement `nose_to_axis`** (`crates/post/src/machine/swing.rs`, `def.rs`, `parse.rs`). This is the spindle nose's height above the rotary's centerline with Z at `safe_retract`.\n  - A rotary turns the work (`AxisLimits::turns_part`) when no `head` part hangs below it. A head tilt, such as `tilthead.mch`, is unaffected.\n  - A garbled value, or the key on any other part, refuses the file by name.\n  - If a work-turning A about X states no `nose_to_axis`, every op is refused by name. The gate has no way to show the turn clears, so it refuses rather than warns.\n- **`tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch`** states `nose_to_axis: 10.6` in. That is Tormach's 770MX 13.75 in spindle nose to table, less the microARC 4's 3.15 in table to centerline (4th-axis comparison sheet 02/24).\n- **Tester kit:** the `.camproj` is re-saved so its embedded machine carries the new facts. The kit `.nc` is byte-identical. README step 3 now says what the gate checks and what is still the operator's job (the chuck and jaws are unmodelled, and the figure comes from the spec sheet).\n- **Docs:** `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` documents the key. The decision record is `docs/decisions/804-a-swept-radius.md`.\n\n## How tested\nNew `crates/app/tests/index_swing.rs` (6 tests):\n- `the_shipped_microarc_states_its_nose_height_and_a_work_turning_a`: also checks that the tilt-head's A turns the tool.\n- `a_short_tool_over_the_kit_bar_clears_and_posts`: the kit's 3/4\" bar with a 3\" tool posts, `G0 A90` included.\n- `a_tool_too_long_to_clear_the_bar_is_refused_by_name`: the clearance is 3 mm against 5. Refused by name, nothing written.\n- `a_fat_chuck_turning_with_the_bar_is_refused_by_name`: a 400 mm turning fixture behind the bar.\n- `a_work_turning_a_with_no_nose_height_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_machine_with_no_a_is_unaffected`: the same too-long tool on the plain 770MX.\n\nUnit tests in `crates/post/src/machine/swing.rs` cover head vs table rotaries and the parse/refusal of `nose_to_axis`.\n\n**Revert check:** with the clause removed from `verification_report`, the three refusal tests fail and the other three pass.\n\nLocal results:\n\n| Suite | Result |\n|---|---|\n| index_swing | 6 passed |\n| tormach_fourth_axis | 12 passed |\n| microarc_test_part | 2 passed (kit `.nc` unchanged) |\n| conformance | 6 passed |\n| posting | 17 passed |\n| tilt | 8 passed |\n| machine | 33 passed |\n| machine_library | 11 passed |\n| machine_edit | 9 passed |\n| project_roundtrip | 71 passed |\n| rotary_letter | 3 passed |\n| rotary_verify | 4 passed |\n| post_not_judged | 12 passed |\n| tormach_post | 10 passed |\n| tormach_safe_retract | 4 passed |\n| camcraft-post (all) | passed |\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. The Linux quick gate (`--base upstream/main`) is running; I'll comment its result.\n\n## Not exercised\n- **Hardware.** Nothing has been run on a 770MX with a microARC 4. The 10.6 in is the spec sheets' nominal figure, not a measurement, and the README still asks the operator to check at the top of Z.\n- **Unmodelled chuck and jaws** are not judged.\n- **Old projects:** a machine embedded in a project saved before this change has no `turns_part`, so it reads as not judged. Reloading the machine fixes it. The only shipped work-turning A is the new microARC file.\n- **Machines pane:** it doesn't expose `nose_to_axis` as a field yet. The key is set in the `.mch` text.\n\nChangelog: The program gate refuses an A index on a work-turning 4th axis (microARC 4) when the retracted tool tip can't clear the swept stock, part and turning fixtures by 5 mm; machine files state the new `nose_to_axis`.\n\n**Changelog note (#813):** this PR also changes behaviour for custom machines. A user's own `.mch` with a table A about X that doesn't state `nose_to_axis` now has every op on that machine refused by name. The cut's changelog row should say so; the wording is in #815's `Changelog:` line.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #804\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
